SHITA SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OOTA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANYO CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAI KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OOTA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OOTA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A nonionic surfactant which is directly produced by causing an aliphatic alcohol (a1) to add an alkylene oxide (b1), is represented by the general formula R&lt;1&gt;O-[(C2H4O)m/(AO)n]-(C2H4O)p-H, and has a value of Mw/Mn in a specific range, and in which the distribution constant c determined using the following equation derived from the Weibull distribution law is 1.0 or smaller. c=(v+n0/n00-1)/[Ln(n00/n0)+n0/n00-1] (4) (In the equation (4), v is the average of (m+n+p) in the above general formula; n00 is the number of moles of the aliphatic alcohol (a1) used in the reaction; and n0 is the number of moles of the aliphatic alcohol (a1) remaining unreacted.) Due to the specific composition and the specific molecular weight, the surfactant is comparable in surface activity to nonionic surfactants of the alkylphenol type and has no fear of generating an endocrine disruptor. A surfactant obtained by making the nonionic surfactant anionic is improved in foaming property and reduced in odor and skin irritation and hence gives an excellent detergent composition.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un tensio-actif non ionique produit directement au moyen d'un alcool aliphatique (a1) traité de sorte qu'il induise l'addition d'oxyde d'alkylène (b1). Ledit tensio-actif est représenté par la formule générale R&lt;1&gt;O-[(CH2H4O)m/(AO)n]-(C2H4O)p-H, et a une valeur de Mw/Mn dans une plage spécifique, et dans laquelle la constante de distribution c déterminée au moyen de l'équation (4) suivante dérivée de a loi de distribution de Weibull est d'au plus 1,0. C=(v+n0/n00-1)/[Ln(n00/n0)+n0/n00-1] (4). [Dans l'équation (4), v représente la moyenne de (m+n+p) dans la formule générale précédente ; n00 représente le nombre de moles d'alcool aliphatique (a1) utilisé dans la réaction ; et n0 représente le nombre de moles d'alcool aliphatique (a1) restant n'ayant pas réagi.] En raison de sa composition spécifique et de son poids moléculaire spécifique, le tensio-actif est comparable, pour ce qui est de son activité de surface, aux tensio-actifs non ioniques du type alkylphénol et n'est pas susceptible de générer de perturbateur du système endocrinien. Un tensio-actif obtenu par transformation du tensio-actif non ionique en tensio-actif ionique présente des propriétés de moussage accrues, une odeur réduite, irrite moins la peau et constitue ainsi une excellente composition détergente.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>